WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.068 --> 00:00:06.584
Hi, welcome back to Nagarjuna.

00:00:06.584 --> 00:00:10.307
We're going to start
with some Sanskrit words

00:00:10.307 --> 00:00:14.907
that are good to know
for the tough task ahead

00:00:14.907 --> 00:00:18.888
of further exploring that special moment

00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:21.745
when everything you need
for something to happen

00:00:21.745 --> 00:00:23.976
has come together,

00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:26.276
and what you want to happen

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:28.406
is about to pop out.

00:00:28.406 --> 00:00:30.856
That point in time...

00:00:30.856 --> 00:00:32.858
We here in the studio,

00:00:32.858 --> 00:00:37.844
we were discussing is there
a good English word for that.

00:00:37.844 --> 00:00:38.775
There were some words,

00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:40.695
there's an idiom, you say
"Everything came together,"

00:00:40.695 --> 00:00:42.541
or something like that.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:44.684
But we don't have a single word for it.

00:00:44.684 --> 00:00:48.729
In Sanskrit, there is
a single word for it.

00:00:48.729 --> 00:00:52.041
And that's 'sāmagryā'. Say sāmagryā.

00:00:52.041 --> 00:00:55.226
- [Students] Sāmagryā.
- Sāmagryā, yeah.

00:00:55.226 --> 00:00:57.226
You can see it here.

00:00:58.874 --> 00:01:01.775
When the causes and
conditions do come together,

00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:04.192
that's called sāmagryā.

00:01:07.351 --> 00:01:08.553
I started to try to work

00:01:08.553 --> 00:01:09.386
on breaking this word down.

00:01:09.386 --> 00:01:13.433
Right, Cristina? This
is what we normally do.

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:18.303
And sāma in Tibetan is
DUMS, DUMS PO,

00:01:18.303 --> 00:01:20.583
which means for everything
to come together.

00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:23.517
So I thought "Oh, here I'm on a roll."

00:01:23.517 --> 00:01:27.874
Sāma is together, so
gryā must be come, or,

00:01:27.874 --> 00:01:31.791
maybe it is related to
@gr - to grab, or to come.

00:01:32.775 --> 00:01:35.899
And then I checked Monier-Williams,

00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:39.026
which is probably the
greatest Sanskrit dictionary

00:01:39.026 --> 00:01:39.986
of all time.

00:01:39.986 --> 00:01:44.699
And he said "No, no, no,
it comes from sam-agra."

00:01:44.699 --> 00:01:46.905
Sam-agra.

00:01:46.905 --> 00:01:51.905
Yeah, Christina, as you just
said, 'agra' means the tip.

00:01:52.568 --> 00:01:57.568
Like the steps of SBYOR LAM -
DROD, RTZE MO, BZOD PA, CHOS CHOG.

00:01:57.581 --> 00:02:01.524
RTZE MO, the second one, or the city Agra,

00:02:01.524 --> 00:02:03.676
where the Taj Mahal is located.

00:02:03.676 --> 00:02:07.242
Agra means the tip or the top point.

00:02:07.242 --> 00:02:10.442
In Monier-Williams it's explained as

00:02:10.442 --> 00:02:12.952
sam-agra.

00:02:12.952 --> 00:02:17.952
So it comes from sam-agra,
'sam' meaning totally,

00:02:18.332 --> 00:02:21.563
and also 'come together',
and then agra means tip,

00:02:21.563 --> 00:02:23.784
which means the pinnacle.

00:02:23.784 --> 00:02:27.551
So think of it as that way:
the pinnacle of readiness

00:02:27.551 --> 00:02:31.202
or the pinnacle of conjunction.

00:02:31.202 --> 00:02:35.043
Because everything came
together perfectly, agra.

00:02:35.043 --> 00:02:35.876
Okay?

00:02:35.876 --> 00:02:38.629
So, he claims it comes from that.

00:02:38.629 --> 00:02:42.072
That would normally be a push
on the way it looks to me,

00:02:42.072 --> 00:02:44.902
but I think it's fine.
It makes a good story,

00:02:44.902 --> 00:02:46.328
as they say.

00:02:46.328 --> 00:02:50.014
And by the way, discussing
these points in Sanskrit

00:02:50.014 --> 00:02:54.192
can be endless over the centuries.

00:02:54.192 --> 00:02:57.688
People have tried over the centuries.

00:02:57.688 --> 00:03:02.688
I think if you find one
that sounds reasonable

00:03:03.075 --> 00:03:07.094
and also tells a story,
or tells a useful point,

00:03:07.094 --> 00:03:08.653
I'll take it.

00:03:08.653 --> 00:03:11.933
If it helps my students
to remember the pieces,

00:03:11.933 --> 00:03:13.516
I'll take it.

00:03:14.407 --> 00:03:16.813
The second word I'd
like you guys to learn,

00:03:16.813 --> 00:03:18.063
is 'phala'.

00:03:18.922 --> 00:03:20.333
Phala.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.583
And in Tibetan it's 'BRAS BU

00:03:23.417 --> 00:03:27.263
The verbal root /phal means to fruit,

00:03:27.263 --> 00:03:29.280
or to ripen as a fruit.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.834
It also means to expand
or burst like a balloon.

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:37.834
And the words full, the
words pure, the word ball,

00:03:37.922 --> 00:03:42.118
the word pore, as in Singapore, Rajapore.

00:03:42.118 --> 00:03:45.002
Singapore means full of lions.

00:03:45.002 --> 00:03:48.533
And then pura became the word for city,

00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:50.493
because it means full of people.

00:03:50.493 --> 00:03:54.934
So, again, P can change
to F, R can change to L,

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:57.152
and you get 'full'.

00:03:57.152 --> 00:03:58.856
From all these: phala.

00:03:58.856 --> 00:04:02.226
The idea of a fruit expanding

00:04:02.226 --> 00:04:06.816
until it's ready to pop open,
and then you bite into it.

00:04:06.816 --> 00:04:07.674
So that's phala.

00:04:07.674 --> 00:04:11.545
In Sanskrit, that's result.

00:04:11.545 --> 00:04:14.056
So, these are going to be
easy to remember, right?

00:04:14.056 --> 00:04:16.385
Sāmagryā,

00:04:16.385 --> 00:04:19.624
the tip of everything coming together.

00:04:19.624 --> 00:04:21.205
And then phala meaning fruit.

00:04:21.205 --> 00:04:24.514
Whoever's outside can come
in, if they're wondering.

00:04:24.514 --> 00:04:27.204
I think it's Jasso.

00:04:30.379 --> 00:04:33.544
Now we've reached another
point in the outline.

00:04:33.544 --> 00:04:36.523
We had already examined,

00:04:36.523 --> 00:04:39.432
is the opening of the
cafe, somehow present

00:04:39.432 --> 00:04:42.720
in the final coming together

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.341
of everything you need to open the cafe?

00:04:45.341 --> 00:04:49.476
We had arguments for
and arguments against.

00:04:49.476 --> 00:04:52.751
And now Choney Lama says,

00:04:52.751 --> 00:04:55.272
the next verse of Nagarjuna,

00:04:55.272 --> 00:04:59.773
you can consider DE LA
YOD MED NYID DGAG PA

00:04:59.773 --> 00:05:03.704
Actually, we just denied
the two possibilities

00:05:03.704 --> 00:05:07.264
that the opening of the cafe was present

00:05:07.264 --> 00:05:09.481
in the coming together
of everything you need

00:05:09.481 --> 00:05:10.704
to open the cafe.

00:05:10.704 --> 00:05:12.624
And we also denied the possibility

00:05:12.624 --> 00:05:14.632
that it wasn't present somehow.

00:05:14.632 --> 00:05:16.133
Or else anything could come out

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:18.282
of all the causes coming together.

00:05:18.282 --> 00:05:22.449
Now, he says "Let's deny
the possibility of both."

00:05:23.499 --> 00:05:26.530
Okay? That it is there
and it isn't there.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.613
Okay?

00:05:27.613 --> 00:05:30.539
So, he changes the wording here.

00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:34.531
He doesn't say, "Does a result

00:05:34.531 --> 00:05:38.072
which is already present
in the conditions arise?"

00:05:38.072 --> 00:05:41.759
Now he just says, "Is
it even a possibility?"

00:05:41.759 --> 00:05:43.274
So a little bit different,

00:05:43.274 --> 00:05:44.650
different shade.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:47.921
We're not discussing "Can
that result pop out?"

00:05:47.921 --> 00:05:51.330
We're discussing does
it even make sense to say

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.200
it does or doesn't exist
at the time of the assembling

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.758
of the conditions?

00:05:56.758 --> 00:05:59.269
Final perfect assembly of the conditions.

00:05:59.269 --> 00:06:03.138
Sāmagryā.

00:06:03.138 --> 00:06:04.501
All right, here we go.

00:06:04.501 --> 00:06:06.026
,GAL TE RGYU DANG RKYEN RNAMS KYI,

00:06:06.026 --> 00:06:07.459
,TSOGS LA 'BRAS BU YOD NA NI,

00:06:07.459 --> 00:06:10.617
,TSOGS LA GZUNG DU YOD RIGS NA,

00:06:10.617 --> 00:06:13.742
,TSOGS PA NYID LA GZUNG DU MED,

00:06:13.742 --> 00:06:15.142
,GAL TE RGYU DANG RKYEN RNAMS KYI,

00:06:15.142 --> 00:06:16.434
,TSOGS LA ‘BRAS BU MED NA NI,

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:18.308
,RGYU RNAMS DANG NI RKYEN DAG KYANG,

00:06:18.308 --> 00:06:20.107
,RGYU RKYEN MA YIN MTSUNGS PAR ‘GYUR,

00:06:21.659 --> 00:06:26.405
And as you see, I'm always...
well, you can't see it here.

00:06:26.405 --> 00:06:28.094
It's an interesting point

00:06:28.094 --> 00:06:31.294
that the version of Nagarjuna
being used by Choney Lama

00:06:31.294 --> 00:06:35.122
is slightly different than
the version of Nagarjuna

00:06:35.122 --> 00:06:39.039
I found in John Brady's
database in the Tengyur.

00:06:39.892 --> 00:06:42.559
So what we have here is probably

00:06:43.962 --> 00:06:48.722
one of the early translations
of an ancient Indian book

00:06:48.722 --> 00:06:51.389
that didn't make it as a choice.

00:06:52.563 --> 00:06:55.874
And Tsongkapa likes to say,

00:06:55.874 --> 00:06:59.964
"I like to read the ones that
didn't make it into the Tengyur

00:06:59.964 --> 00:07:01.692
because sometimes they're better."

00:07:01.692 --> 00:07:04.914
Or sometimes some of
the verses are better.

00:07:04.914 --> 00:07:06.583
So you can imagine.

00:07:06.583 --> 00:07:10.914
50 years from now, people trying to choose

00:07:10.914 --> 00:07:15.049
which translation of this book
is going to be the standard.

00:07:15.049 --> 00:07:18.012
Whichever they choose, is
going to have some weaknesses

00:07:18.012 --> 00:07:21.268
that were not present in
some of the alternatives.

00:07:21.268 --> 00:07:23.061
And what we have here,

00:07:23.061 --> 00:07:25.644
if you're really a textual nerd,

00:07:26.919 --> 00:07:31.919
you have a version that
was popular somehow

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:36.463
even before the final decision was made.

00:07:36.463 --> 00:07:38.674
There are some interesting differences

00:07:38.674 --> 00:07:42.499
and they tell stories.

00:07:43.864 --> 00:07:45.884
They're profitable to study,

00:07:45.884 --> 00:07:50.408
if you have lots of free time.
[students giggle]

00:07:50.408 --> 00:07:52.311
But if people are texting you all morning

00:07:52.311 --> 00:07:55.853
it's not probable.
[students giggle]

00:07:56.995 --> 00:07:58.361
GZHAN YANG GAL TE RGYU DANG RKYEN

00:07:58.361 --> 00:07:59.584
RNAMS KYI TSOGS PA LA 'BRAS BU BRTEN PA'I

00:07:59.584 --> 00:08:00.417
SGO NAS YOD NA NI

00:08:00.417 --> 00:08:01.717
Now he says...

00:08:04.296 --> 00:08:06.743
Let's not discuss whether or not

00:08:06.743 --> 00:08:09.525
the opening of the cafe is present

00:08:09.525 --> 00:08:13.274
in the convening of everything
you need to open the cafe,

00:08:13.274 --> 00:08:16.645
like a jewel in a ring.

00:08:16.645 --> 00:08:18.973
Let's not look at it that way.

00:08:18.973 --> 00:08:21.173
Let's look at it this way.

00:08:21.173 --> 00:08:23.783
Is it present in an implied way,

00:08:23.783 --> 00:08:26.373
in that it leans upon the convening

00:08:26.373 --> 00:08:27.852
of the causes and conditions?

00:08:27.852 --> 00:08:30.933
It rests upon or it depends upon

00:08:30.933 --> 00:08:31.782
the convening of...

00:08:31.782 --> 00:08:36.102
So let's not say it's nested
in the causes and conditions.

00:08:36.102 --> 00:08:39.251
Let's looks at whether it can rely on

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:40.284
the causes and conditions.

00:08:40.284 --> 00:08:42.433
If it can lean on the
causes and conditions.

00:08:42.433 --> 00:08:44.593
Can it be present in the sense

00:08:44.593 --> 00:08:46.873
of leaning on the causes and conditions?

00:08:46.873 --> 00:08:48.661
So it's a little bit different, right?

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:52.382
Not -- is it present nested in
the causes and conditions? 

00:08:52.382 --> 00:08:55.454
Is it present leaning on
the causes and conditions?

00:08:55.454 --> 00:08:58.346
So that's what we're going to look at now.

00:08:59.991 --> 00:09:00.824
GAL TE RGYU DANG RKYEN RNAMS KYI

00:09:00.824 --> 00:09:02.313
TSOGS LA 'BRAS BU MED NA NI

00:09:02.313 --> 00:09:03.646
I'm sorry.

00:09:05.481 --> 00:09:06.314
GAL TE RGYU DANG RKYEN RNAMS KYI TSOGS PA LA

00:09:06.314 --> 00:09:07.147
‘BRAS BU BRTEN PA’I SGO NAS 

00:09:07.147 --> 00:09:08.960
YOD NA NI MI ‘THAD DE,

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.572
If you say the result is present

00:09:12.572 --> 00:09:15.982
in the convening of all the
necessary causes and conditions,

00:09:15.982 --> 00:09:18.882
in the sense of leaning on them,

00:09:18.882 --> 00:09:22.922
DE YIN NA TSOGS PA LA 'BRAS BU
DNGOS SU GZUNG DU YOD RIGS NA

00:09:22.922 --> 00:09:26.922
in that case, it should
be, somehow detectable

00:09:28.806 --> 00:09:31.438
in the causes and conditions.

00:09:31.438 --> 00:09:34.036
If it were leaning on the
causes and conditions,

00:09:34.036 --> 00:09:37.694
if it were present in the sense

00:09:37.694 --> 00:09:41.025
of the glass resting upon the table,

00:09:41.025 --> 00:09:43.825
then it should somehow be perceivable

00:09:43.825 --> 00:09:45.591
in the causes and conditions.

00:09:45.591 --> 00:09:48.584
If it were the necessary appendage

00:09:48.584 --> 00:09:51.549
of the causes and conditions,

00:09:51.549 --> 00:09:53.556
then when you saw the
causes and conditions,

00:09:53.556 --> 00:09:57.308
you should somehow be
able to see the result

00:09:57.308 --> 00:09:59.787
that's going to come out of
the causes and conditions.

00:09:59.787 --> 00:10:03.907
It should be present like
a cup resting on the table.

00:10:03.907 --> 00:10:06.949
He says, "But that's not right."

00:10:06.949 --> 00:10:08.824
DE YIN NA TSOGS PA LA 'BRAS BU DNGOS SU

00:10:08.824 --> 00:10:10.819
GZUNG DU YOD RIGS NA

00:10:10.819 --> 00:10:15.105
If it were present in the act of leaning

00:10:15.105 --> 00:10:17.707
on the causes and conditions or resting

00:10:17.707 --> 00:10:22.128
on the causes and conditions,
then it should be detectable

00:10:22.128 --> 00:10:23.785
by some correct perception, right?

00:10:23.785 --> 00:10:25.938
We said that was the
definition of existence.

00:10:25.938 --> 00:10:28.262
But it's not.

00:10:28.262 --> 00:10:30.474
There's no way you can perceive

00:10:30.474 --> 00:10:34.312
the actual operating cafe in the presence

00:10:34.312 --> 00:10:39.255
of the building, and the
capital, and the uncooked food.

00:10:39.255 --> 00:10:43.929
You see what I mean? You cannot see it.

00:10:43.929 --> 00:10:47.890
It's not observable in
the causes and conditions

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:49.390
before it pops up.

00:10:51.194 --> 00:10:53.726
So cancel that idea.

00:10:53.726 --> 00:10:55.925
Now, how is he going to go next?

00:10:55.925 --> 00:10:56.758
You tell me.

00:10:56.758 --> 00:10:58.219
I'll say what he said so far,

00:10:58.219 --> 00:11:02.823
you tell me what he's going to say next.

00:11:02.823 --> 00:11:06.611
Is the opening of the cafe present

00:11:06.611 --> 00:11:11.081
in all the conditions and
causes for it to open

00:11:11.081 --> 00:11:14.880
in a way that it leans on
them or it is resting on them?

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:17.472
And you say, "No." And I say, "Why?"

00:11:17.472 --> 00:11:18.930
And you say, "Because we can't observe it

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:21.268
at that point in time."

00:11:21.268 --> 00:11:25.226
Then I say, "Then what
will Nagarjuna do next?"

00:11:25.226 --> 00:11:26.167
What?

00:11:26.167 --> 00:11:27.267
[student speaks off mic]

00:11:27.267 --> 00:11:29.225
Yeah, are they disconnected?

00:11:29.225 --> 00:11:32.518
Is it not resting on the
causes and conditions?

00:11:32.518 --> 00:11:35.251
Then he says, GAL TE RGYU DANG RKYEN

00:11:35.251 --> 00:11:37.784
RNAMS KYI TSOGS PA LA 'BRAS BU
MED NA YANG NI MI 'THAD DE

00:11:37.784 --> 00:11:39.358
MED NA YANG means,

00:11:39.358 --> 00:11:41.855
And if it's not leaning on
the causes and conditions,

00:11:41.855 --> 00:11:44.431
or if it's not present there resting

00:11:44.431 --> 00:11:48.170
on the causes and conditions,
it's also impossible.

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:52.120
Right? It's that Nagarjunian options.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.944
Both options are impossible.

00:11:54.944 --> 00:11:56.631
We need a...

00:11:56.631 --> 00:11:58.481
Give me the Tibetan word for $100.

00:11:58.481 --> 00:11:59.508
PHUN GSUM PA

00:11:59.508 --> 00:12:00.341
PHUN GSUM PA

00:12:00.341 --> 00:12:02.494
Oh my God.
[students Chattering]

00:12:02.494 --> 00:12:04.418
Connie, $100.

00:12:04.418 --> 00:12:07.118
Collect it from Jigme
when she comes back, okay?

00:12:07.118 --> 00:12:11.081
She's visiting her relatives in California

00:12:11.081 --> 00:12:12.871
from Holland.

00:12:12.871 --> 00:12:13.704
Okay, so...

00:12:15.868 --> 00:12:20.268
It's also incorrect to say
that the opening of the cafe

00:12:20.268 --> 00:12:22.908
is not resting upon the
causes and conditions

00:12:22.908 --> 00:12:25.145
in the time of the causes and conditions

00:12:25.145 --> 00:12:27.078
because MYU GU LTA BU'I RGYU RNAMS

00:12:27.078 --> 00:12:30.061
DANG NI RKYEN DAG KYANG
DE'I RGYU RKYEN MA YIN PA

00:12:30.956 --> 00:12:33.421
Then there would be no
necessary relationship

00:12:33.421 --> 00:12:36.721
between the opening of the cafe

00:12:36.721 --> 00:12:39.771
and the conditions for
the opening of the cafe

00:12:39.771 --> 00:12:41.354
if the opening of the cafe

00:12:41.354 --> 00:12:43.267
were not necessarily dependent

00:12:43.267 --> 00:12:45.615
of those causes and conditions.

00:12:45.615 --> 00:12:47.032
And in that case

00:12:49.642 --> 00:12:51.850
he says, "you could use..."

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.850
Take the picture, Tim.

00:12:55.305 --> 00:12:57.542
"You can use a lump of coal
[students giggling]

00:12:57.542 --> 00:12:59.755
to open the cafe."

00:12:59.755 --> 00:13:02.632
Apparently in Tibet, this is like,

00:13:02.632 --> 00:13:05.345
if you want to give an example

00:13:05.345 --> 00:13:08.857
of some ridiculous thing
that could be the cause

00:13:08.857 --> 00:13:10.495
of what you're talking about,

00:13:10.495 --> 00:13:12.932
if that wasn't the cause
as it was supposed to be,

00:13:12.932 --> 00:13:16.419
you'd say... I'd say rabbit
turd, or something like that.

00:13:16.419 --> 00:13:19.032
He said lump of coal.

00:13:19.032 --> 00:13:22.449
RDO SOL, RDO SOL, which you'll never see.

00:13:23.941 --> 00:13:27.391
RDO SOL means coal rock.

00:13:27.391 --> 00:13:29.391
Then a coal rock should...

00:13:32.328 --> 00:13:37.311
Then coal rocks... then
ready to operate...I'm sorry

00:13:38.518 --> 00:13:40.728
Operating cafes...

00:13:40.728 --> 00:13:43.453
Cafes on their opening day should pop out

00:13:43.453 --> 00:13:47.366
of random coal rocks laying
around on the ground

00:13:47.366 --> 00:13:51.388
if there didn't have to be
some relationship between them.

00:13:51.388 --> 00:13:53.263
Got it?

00:13:54.116 --> 00:13:56.594
All right we got through
that one. God bless.

00:13:56.594 --> 00:13:58.581
Let's see if it gets easier.

00:13:58.581 --> 00:14:00.394
You're always hoping it gets easier
and easier and it doesn't.

00:14:00.394 --> 00:14:03.706
By the time you're hoping it
gets easier it's hopeless.

00:14:03.706 --> 00:14:04.539
Okay.

00:14:06.756 --> 00:14:10.173
BRGYUD NAS SKYE BA DGAG PA

00:14:11.569 --> 00:14:14.667
If the result of the cafe opening

00:14:14.667 --> 00:14:18.569
doesn't pop directly out of
the causes and conditions

00:14:18.569 --> 00:14:21.369
coming together, is it a possibility

00:14:21.369 --> 00:14:24.835
that it pops out indirectly?

00:14:27.106 --> 00:14:28.244
I'll say it again.

00:14:28.244 --> 00:14:32.181
If it's not the case that
the open cafe pops out

00:14:32.181 --> 00:14:34.804
of the coming together of
the causes and conditions

00:14:34.804 --> 00:14:36.956
for the opening of the cafe,

00:14:36.956 --> 00:14:40.268
then can the causes and
conditions coming together

00:14:40.268 --> 00:14:44.675
somehow in time create
the opening of the cafe?

00:14:44.675 --> 00:14:47.891
Meaning after some time has passed.

00:14:47.891 --> 00:14:50.494
Is there somehow an interim period

00:14:50.494 --> 00:14:54.306
between the convening of the
necessary causes and conditions

00:14:54.306 --> 00:14:57.544
and the popping up of the cafe,

00:14:57.544 --> 00:14:59.692
where we could get the cinnamon rolls?

00:14:59.692 --> 00:15:01.769
Connie's ultimate challenge:

00:15:01.769 --> 00:15:02.929
[students laugh]

00:15:02.929 --> 00:15:07.229
make the same taste with
all healthy ingredients

00:15:07.229 --> 00:15:10.106
as the signature product of the cafe.

00:15:10.106 --> 00:15:11.892
[students Laugh]

00:15:11.892 --> 00:15:15.491
I just see JB like a chemist, mad chemist,

00:15:15.491 --> 00:15:18.408
With his, what's that sugar called?,

00:15:19.889 --> 00:15:22.628
Monk's Fruit sugar,
trying to get the taste

00:15:22.628 --> 00:15:25.939
of a cinnamon roll.

00:15:25.939 --> 00:15:28.603
The odds are not very great.

00:15:28.603 --> 00:15:29.853
Here we go.

00:15:29.853 --> 00:15:31.087
Here's the verse.

00:15:31.087 --> 00:15:35.095
,GAL TE RGYU YIS 'BRAS BU LA,
,RGYU BYIN NAS NI 'GAG 'GYUR NA,

00:15:35.095 --> 00:15:42.244
,GANG BYIN PA DANG GANG 'GAGS PA'I,
,RGYU YI BDAG NYID GNYIS SU 'GYUR,

00:15:42.244 --> 00:15:46.128
,GAL TE RGYU YIS ‘BRAS BU LA,
,RGYU MA BYIN PAR ‘GAG ‘GYUR NA,

00:15:46.128 --> 00:15:50.756
,RGYU ‘GAGS NAS NI SKYES PA YI,
,’BRAS BU DE DAG RGYU MED ‘GYUR,

00:15:50.756 --> 00:15:52.103
What time we stop, Tim?

00:15:52.103 --> 00:15:52.936
Sorry.

00:15:53.936 --> 00:15:56.183
Yeah, in four...

00:15:56.183 --> 00:15:59.020
30 minutes from now, five o'clock.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:00.193
Okay, good.

00:16:00.193 --> 00:16:02.318
All right, here we go.

00:16:02.318 --> 00:16:05.820
Now, to understand or
to appreciate this verse,

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.793
can you bring the verse back?

00:16:07.793 --> 00:16:11.720
I want you to appreciate
a certain word here,

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:14.504
which is BYIN.

00:16:14.504 --> 00:16:16.957
It's the second word
here in the second line,

00:16:16.957 --> 00:16:19.856
and it's the second
word in the third line.

00:16:19.856 --> 00:16:21.370
BYIN

00:16:24.383 --> 00:16:27.469
BYIN is obviously
related to the word give.

00:16:27.469 --> 00:16:29.293
So the name of the first perfection

00:16:29.293 --> 00:16:31.716
of the six bodhisattva perfections

00:16:31.716 --> 00:16:33.343
is SBYIN PA,

00:16:33.343 --> 00:16:36.170
which is giving with an
S in front of it.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:38.433
But here you just got BYIN.

00:16:38.433 --> 00:16:43.018
And this is a very
unique usage of the verb

00:16:43.018 --> 00:16:45.518
that means to

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.693
to spit out a result.

00:16:49.606 --> 00:16:52.106
It means to spit out a result.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:58.341
And it's also the verb that you use

00:16:58.341 --> 00:17:00.766
for distilling medicines

00:17:00.766 --> 00:17:03.256
from herbs, from medicinal herbs.

00:17:03.256 --> 00:17:04.430
It's called BYIN.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:07.477
So somehow you boil the herbs

00:17:07.477 --> 00:17:12.471
and then they BYIN the...
they yield this special...

00:17:13.498 --> 00:17:17.481
They give forth this medicinal liquid.

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:22.160
Then you throw out

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:26.418
the herbs that you
distilled the liquid from.

00:17:26.418 --> 00:17:29.546
Those thrown out herbs

00:17:29.546 --> 00:17:33.713
are allowed to monks and nuns.

00:17:35.133 --> 00:17:38.133
They have to search the garbage cans

00:17:40.629 --> 00:17:42.046
for the used husks.

00:17:43.316 --> 00:17:46.240
And they're not allowed to wear new cloth

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:47.151
and things like that.

00:17:47.151 --> 00:17:49.336
They're supposed to live off of

00:17:49.336 --> 00:17:52.336
what has the society has thrown out.

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:56.473
It's a pretty cool idea, actually.

00:17:58.724 --> 00:18:00.391
So get this feeling.

00:18:01.725 --> 00:18:03.776
When you're talking about cause and effect

00:18:03.776 --> 00:18:06.276
what would the word BYIN mean?

00:18:07.838 --> 00:18:09.326
Or when you're talking
about the convergence

00:18:09.326 --> 00:18:14.326
of causes and conditions,
what would the word BYIN mean?

00:18:14.813 --> 00:18:18.052
It spit out the open cafe.

00:18:18.052 --> 00:18:23.003
The open cafe squirted
out, like the medicine

00:18:23.003 --> 00:18:24.580
out of the herbs,

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:27.393
after they're boiled, as they're boiled.

00:18:27.393 --> 00:18:30.643
So try to get in your mind this concept

00:18:31.893 --> 00:18:35.201
that maybe has no
particular word in English

00:18:35.201 --> 00:18:38.118
of causes and conditions assembling

00:18:39.953 --> 00:18:42.870
in the final moment, and then poof,

00:18:46.239 --> 00:18:49.190
they spit out a cafe on the opening day.

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.023
Okay?

00:18:52.416 --> 00:18:54.993
And we're going to talk
about the status of the cause

00:18:54.993 --> 00:18:57.956
before the spitting, during the spitting,

00:18:57.956 --> 00:18:59.873
and after the spitting.

00:19:01.993 --> 00:19:03.530
We're going to talk about the status

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.693
of the causes and conditions
that came together

00:19:06.693 --> 00:19:09.930
after they have spit out the finished cafe,

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:13.170
or as they're spitting
out the finished cafe,

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.743
or even after.

00:19:15.743 --> 00:19:17.326
Did I say after?

00:19:17.326 --> 00:19:19.003
Or before.

00:19:19.003 --> 00:19:19.920
Here we go.

00:19:21.653 --> 00:19:23.619
GAL TE RGYUS RANG GI 'BRAS BU LA DNGOS

00:19:23.619 --> 00:19:25.944
SU SKYED PA'I NUS PA BYIN NAS

00:19:25.944 --> 00:19:28.016
'BRAS BU'I SNGAR 'GAGS PAS

00:19:28.016 --> 00:19:29.349
If it's the case

00:19:32.064 --> 00:19:33.314
that the cause,

00:19:36.526 --> 00:19:37.726
I don't know how to say it,

00:19:37.726 --> 00:19:40.309
if it's the case that the cause

00:19:41.916 --> 00:19:45.590
exhibits its power to
produce something.

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:48.173
If it's the case that the cause

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:54.103
ejects the result,

00:19:54.103 --> 00:19:58.853
spits out the result, 
NUS PA BYIN NAS

00:20:02.353 --> 00:20:05.020
and then wears itself out, okay?

00:20:06.516 --> 00:20:08.130
Here we go.

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:12.830
Is it the case that once
the causes and conditions

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:17.830
for the cafe to open have spit out a cafe

00:20:18.293 --> 00:20:19.716
on the opening day,

00:20:19.716 --> 00:20:21.716
then do they exhaust themselves?

00:20:24.114 --> 00:20:26.703
And it says, "Yes." I
mean those particular...

00:20:26.703 --> 00:20:28.380
he money that you saved

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:29.930
for the opening on the first day

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:34.903
has spit out the cafe, and
when the cafe is there

00:20:34.903 --> 00:20:37.216
that money is gone already.

00:20:37.216 --> 00:20:38.780
So is it the case

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:43.780
that in the direct
production of the result,

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:48.303
the cause has worn itself out,

00:20:48.303 --> 00:20:51.866
has exhausted itself before the result?

00:20:51.866 --> 00:20:52.699
Or when?

00:20:56.179 --> 00:20:59.834
- [Student] After?
- After the result?

00:20:59.834 --> 00:21:01.097
He's asking,

00:21:01.097 --> 00:21:03.259
'BRAS BU'I SNGAR 'GAGS PAS

00:21:03.259 --> 00:21:07.810
Let's say that the BYIN
power, the production power,

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:11.037
spitting out power of
the seed it has exhausted

00:21:11.037 --> 00:21:13.171
by the time the cafe opens.

00:21:13.171 --> 00:21:14.004
Let's say that.

00:21:14.004 --> 00:21:17.279
'GAGS PAS SNGAR GYI RIGS PAS MI GNOD DO

00:21:17.279 --> 00:21:19.110
This is the other guy.

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:21.067
He says "Look, I don't see

00:21:21.067 --> 00:21:24.244
why you have a problem, Nagarjuna."

00:21:24.244 --> 00:21:26.416
When all the money, and all the workers,

00:21:26.416 --> 00:21:31.416
and all the uncooked food has
come together, and spit out

00:21:31.426 --> 00:21:35.927
the cafe on the first day
of the cafe's opening,

00:21:35.927 --> 00:21:39.840
then yeah, they have used up
their power by definition.

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:42.542
That's what causes do.

00:21:42.542 --> 00:21:45.629
They wear themselves out
by creating their results.

00:21:45.629 --> 00:21:47.766
He says, "I don't see a problem."

00:21:47.766 --> 00:21:51.867
That's his position. What's
Nagarjuna's position?

00:21:51.867 --> 00:21:54.717
GAL TE RGYU YIS NI 'BRAS BU LA BYED RGYU

00:21:54.717 --> 00:21:57.176
BYIN NAS NI 'GAG PAR 'GYUR NA

00:21:57.176 --> 00:22:02.141
If the cause exhausts itself
in producing the result,

00:22:02.141 --> 00:22:04.707
'BRAS BU LA GANG BYIN PA'I

00:22:04.707 --> 00:22:08.182
BYED RGYU DANG GANG ZHIG 'GAGS PA'I

00:22:08.182 --> 00:22:11.342
RGYU YI BDAG NYID GNYIS SU
RDZAS SO SO BAR 'GYUR NA

00:22:11.342 --> 00:22:16.342
Then in that case, the
cafe that was spit out

00:22:16.854 --> 00:22:20.529
and the cause that spit it out

00:22:20.529 --> 00:22:23.792
can no longer have a relationship,

00:22:23.792 --> 00:22:28.792
because the causes used
themselves up to spit it up.

00:22:29.565 --> 00:22:31.882
A cause that has exhausted itself

00:22:31.882 --> 00:22:34.319
and therefore gone out of existence

00:22:34.319 --> 00:22:37.369
cannot have a relationship
with an open cafe.

00:22:39.171 --> 00:22:41.381
All right? Got it? [Laughs]

00:22:41.381 --> 00:22:49.504
BYIN PA'I BYED RGYU DANG GANG ZHIG
'GAGS PA' RGYU YI BDAG NYID GNYIS SU
RDZAS SO SO BAR 'GYUR NA DE MI RIGS
TE, DE GNYIS KA'ANG RGYUR MTSUNG
PAS 'BRAS BU'I SNGAR 'GAG DZOG PAR

00:22:49.504 --> 00:22:54.504
If the result somehow had to
make contact with the cause

00:22:55.103 --> 00:22:58.314
that had worn itself out, then the result

00:22:58.314 --> 00:23:00.981
should have worn itself out also.

00:23:04.504 --> 00:23:05.379
I'll say it again.

00:23:05.379 --> 00:23:10.066
If the finished result
somehow has a relationship

00:23:10.066 --> 00:23:14.266
with a seed, or a convening
of causes and conditions,

00:23:14.266 --> 00:23:16.802
which has already worn
itself out, then something

00:23:16.802 --> 00:23:20.139
that does exist is having a relationship

00:23:20.139 --> 00:23:21.797
with something that no longer exist.

00:23:21.797 --> 00:23:24.052
And that's not possible.

00:23:24.052 --> 00:23:28.326
If the cause uses itself
up to produce the result,

00:23:28.326 --> 00:23:31.000
that's illogical, because the result

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:33.139
could never have contact with the cause

00:23:33.139 --> 00:23:34.526
because the cause would be gone

00:23:34.526 --> 00:23:37.077
by the time the result occurs.

00:23:37.077 --> 00:23:40.216
Then there would be no cause and effect.

00:23:40.216 --> 00:23:44.776
And then our lump of
coal could open the cafe.

00:23:44.776 --> 00:23:49.252
Because there's no
connection there either.

00:23:49.252 --> 00:23:50.652
Everything that didn't have a connection

00:23:50.652 --> 00:23:52.626
could cause the cafe to open.

00:23:52.626 --> 00:23:54.126
That's what we're really hoping.

00:23:54.126 --> 00:23:58.452
[students and instructor laugh]

00:23:59.602 --> 00:24:01.843
All right.

00:24:05.721 --> 00:24:08.992
DE GNYIS KA'ANG RGYUR MTSUNG PAS

00:24:08.992 --> 00:24:10.766
Yea and he further says

00:24:10.766 --> 00:24:14.264
that the other option
is that in the moment

00:24:14.264 --> 00:24:16.692
that it would spit out, the result ended

00:24:16.692 --> 00:24:20.775
because it was spit
out by an ending cause.

00:24:24.792 --> 00:24:29.792
And only things of the same
nature can touch each other.

00:24:29.992 --> 00:24:34.016
So if the cause exhausts
itself to produce the result,

00:24:34.016 --> 00:24:36.516
then if they have contact,

00:24:36.516 --> 00:24:38.756
if that particular
result could have contact

00:24:38.756 --> 00:24:40.453
with that particular kind of cause,

00:24:40.453 --> 00:24:41.706
then that would have to be a result

00:24:41.706 --> 00:24:43.242
that was blinking out of existence

00:24:43.242 --> 00:24:45.529
even as it came into existence.

00:24:45.529 --> 00:24:48.542
because that's what its brother is doing.

00:24:48.542 --> 00:24:51.209
and they are holding hands.

00:24:55.592 --> 00:24:57.692
I'm not even going to
try the picture, okay?

00:24:57.692 --> 00:24:59.632
Give it up, Tim.

00:24:59.632 --> 00:25:00.565
Okay.

00:25:00.565 --> 00:25:02.323
GAL TE RGYU YIS NI
'BRAS BU LA BYED RGYU MA

00:25:02.323 --> 00:25:04.214
BYIN PAR SNGA LOGS NAS
'GAG PAR 'GYUR NA NI

00:25:04.214 --> 00:25:06.497
MI 'THAD DE, RGYU 'GAGS
PA'I RJES NAS NI SKYES PA

00:25:06.497 --> 00:25:08.897
YI 'BRAS BU MYU GU
LTA BU DE DAG NI RGYU LAS

00:25:08.897 --> 00:25:11.272
DNGOS SU MI SKYE BA KHO
NAR 'GYUR BAS RGYU MED DU

00:25:11.272 --> 00:25:14.688
'BYUNG BAR 'GYUR BA'I SKYON YOD BA'I PHYIR

00:25:18.955 --> 00:25:21.880
GAL TE RGYU YIS NI 'BRAS BU
LA BYED RGYU MA BYIN PAR

00:25:22.922 --> 00:25:27.922
Now if the cause could produce the result

00:25:28.902 --> 00:25:32.069
before the cause had exhausted itself.

00:25:34.002 --> 00:25:34.835
Okay?

00:25:34.835 --> 00:25:37.266
If the cause could produce the result

00:25:37.266 --> 00:25:41.129
before it had exhausted
itself in the producing.

00:25:41.129 --> 00:25:43.729
There's a problem if
it exhausts itself totally

00:25:43.729 --> 00:25:44.816
in the producing

00:25:44.816 --> 00:25:49.307
because then the result doesn't
have anybody to connect with.

00:25:49.307 --> 00:25:50.854
So maybe the other guy is going to say,

00:25:50.854 --> 00:25:53.619
"You know what? Most of the
causes wears itself out

00:25:53.619 --> 00:25:56.232
and then the result happens."

00:25:56.232 --> 00:25:58.231
So then there's still a relationship.

00:25:58.231 --> 00:26:02.430
There's still some cause
there to have relationship.

00:26:02.430 --> 00:26:03.263
'BRAS BU MYU GU LTA BU DE
DAG NI RGYU LAS DNGOS SU

00:26:03.263 --> 00:26:04.096
MI SKYE BA KHO NAR 'GYUR
BAS RGYU MED DU 'BYUNG BAR

00:26:04.096 --> 00:26:06.045
'GYUR BA'I SKYON YOD BA'I PHYIR TE,

00:26:06.045 --> 00:26:08.653
RGYU MED DU 'BYUNG BAR

00:26:10.346 --> 00:26:15.338
Then, somehow if the cause
were to disappear before it,

00:26:16.906 --> 00:26:19.114
before the result was all the way out?

00:26:19.114 --> 00:26:20.480
RGYU 'GAGS PA'I RJES NAS NI SKYES PA YI

00:26:20.480 --> 00:26:21.313
'BRAS BU MYU GU LTA BU DE DAG NI RGYU LAS

00:26:21.313 --> 00:26:26.121
DNGOS SU MI SKYE BA KHO NAR 'GYUR BAS

00:26:27.206 --> 00:26:29.295
In that... I'm sorry.

00:26:29.295 --> 00:26:31.046
Let's say it in a different way.

00:26:31.046 --> 00:26:33.856
If the cause exhausted
itself, there was a break,

00:26:33.856 --> 00:26:37.619
and then the result came
out, that's also impossible.

00:26:37.619 --> 00:26:42.046
If the cause exhausts
itself, takes a break,

00:26:42.046 --> 00:26:44.632
and then the result comes
out, that's also impossible

00:26:44.632 --> 00:26:49.599
because something like
the sprout coming out

00:26:54.231 --> 00:26:58.826
would have to arise without
the presence of the cause.

00:26:58.826 --> 00:27:01.576
The sprout would have to come out

00:27:02.530 --> 00:27:04.346
after a moment has passed,

00:27:04.346 --> 00:27:09.346
in which the seed already disappeared.

00:27:09.369 --> 00:27:11.202
It would have to be a gap.

00:27:12.355 --> 00:27:14.443
RGYU MED DU ‘BYUNG BAR ‘GYUR BA’I 
SKYON YOD BA’I PHYIR TE,

00:27:14.443 --> 00:27:17.626
Why? ‘BRAS BU DANG RGYU ‘GAGS PA 
RANG BZHIN GYIS GRUB NA 

00:27:23.579 --> 00:27:26.609
If the stopping of the result
and the stopping of the cause

00:27:26.609 --> 00:27:28.392
existed by nature,

00:27:28.392 --> 00:27:32.341
RGYU LA BRTEN PA YANG RANG
BZHIN GYIS YOD DGOS LA,

00:27:34.458 --> 00:27:38.975
YOD NA 'BRAS BU DE 'BYUNG BA YANG
RGYU MED DU 'BYUNG RIGS PA'I PHYIR,

00:27:38.975 --> 00:27:42.095
‘BRAS BU DANG RGYU ‘GAGS PA 
RANG BZHIN GYIS GRUB NA

00:27:42.095 --> 00:27:45.185
If the ending of the cause
and the ending of the result

00:27:45.185 --> 00:27:47.743
existed from their own side,

00:27:47.743 --> 00:27:50.845
DE RGYU LA BRTEN PA YANG

00:27:50.845 --> 00:27:55.022
then the relying of the
result on the cause,

00:27:55.022 --> 00:27:56.827
RANG BZHIN GYIS YOD DGOS LA

00:27:56.827 --> 00:27:59.758
that relationship would
have to exist by nature.

00:27:59.758 --> 00:28:01.535
YOD NA 
If the relationship

00:28:01.535 --> 00:28:04.643
between the result and the
cause existed by nature,

00:28:04.643 --> 00:28:07.285
'BRAS BU DE 'BYUNG BA YANG RGYU MED DU

00:28:07.285 --> 00:28:08.577
'BYUNG RIGS PA'I PHYIR,

00:28:08.577 --> 00:28:12.145
then the result could
happen without the cause.

00:28:12.145 --> 00:28:14.485
If the relationship existed by nature,

00:28:14.485 --> 00:28:17.059
because then the result
would exist by nature

00:28:17.059 --> 00:28:18.642
and existing by nature

00:28:18.642 --> 00:28:22.809
implies that you don't
depend on some other thing.

00:28:25.962 --> 00:28:27.895
DE LTAR NA RGYU 'GAGS ZIN NAS 'BRAS BU

00:28:27.895 --> 00:28:30.375
SKYE DGOS NA DE MI 'THAD DE,

00:28:30.375 --> 00:28:31.875
Therefore, it's illogical to say

00:28:31.875 --> 00:28:34.362
that the cause has worn itself out

00:28:34.362 --> 00:28:37.112
and then the result came,

00:28:37.112 --> 00:28:40.212
after the cause has worn itself out. Why?

00:28:40.212 --> 00:28:41.612
RGYU 'GAGS ZIN PA DANG 'BRAS BU SKYES

00:28:41.612 --> 00:28:44.778
ZIN PA GNYIS DUS MNYAM PA'I PHYIR,

00:28:44.778 --> 00:28:46.594
Because in that case

00:28:46.594 --> 00:28:48.625
the time of the exhausting of the cause

00:28:48.625 --> 00:28:50.935
and the time of the
wearing out of the result

00:28:50.935 --> 00:28:53.095
should be simultaneous,

00:28:53.095 --> 00:28:58.095
because they have a relationship:

00:28:58.552 --> 00:29:03.545
one must be present when
the other is present.

00:29:03.545 --> 00:29:06.182
Do the cause and effect
have a relationship? Yes.

00:29:06.182 --> 00:29:08.545
Should one be present
when the other is present?

00:29:08.545 --> 00:29:10.608
Yes, you can't have a relationship

00:29:10.608 --> 00:29:13.146
if two people are not
in the room together.

00:29:13.146 --> 00:29:17.607
Well, is the cause wearing
itself out at that moment?

00:29:17.607 --> 00:29:20.947
Yes. So, okay, the result
is also wearing itself out.

00:29:20.947 --> 00:29:23.869
So in the final moment of
the cause doing its thing,

00:29:23.869 --> 00:29:27.119
the result will blink out of existence.

00:29:28.468 --> 00:29:31.580
Why? They're holding
hands in the same room.

00:29:31.580 --> 00:29:33.980
It can't be that the cause disappears

00:29:33.980 --> 00:29:35.550
and then the result appears

00:29:35.550 --> 00:29:38.230
because there would be
nobody to hold hands with.

00:29:38.230 --> 00:29:39.728
So if it's the case that the cause

00:29:39.728 --> 00:29:41.954
is wearing itself out
to produce the result,

00:29:41.954 --> 00:29:44.214
then the result would have
to be wearing itself out

00:29:44.214 --> 00:29:46.889
at the same time that the
cause is wearing itself out.

00:29:46.889 --> 00:29:51.889
And they should both pop out
of existence at the same time.

00:29:54.152 --> 00:29:54.985
Okay!

00:29:56.501 --> 00:29:58.851
Something easier now.

00:29:58.851 --> 00:30:00.411
I promise.

00:30:00.411 --> 00:30:05.287
The whole structure of this chapter was,

00:30:05.287 --> 00:30:06.867
I don't know if you remember

00:30:06.867 --> 00:30:09.450
because it was a long time ago,

00:30:11.737 --> 00:30:16.636
does the perfect convention,
convening of causes

00:30:16.636 --> 00:30:21.544
and conditions occur
before result pops out,

00:30:22.911 --> 00:30:27.374
or somehow simultaneous
to the result popping out,

00:30:27.374 --> 00:30:29.811
or somehow does the
result popped out first

00:30:29.811 --> 00:30:32.000
and then they convene?

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:34.638
Three possibilities, right?

00:30:34.638 --> 00:30:36.588
We're going on to the second possibility,

00:30:36.588 --> 00:30:37.724
which is what?

00:30:37.724 --> 00:30:40.311
They are simultaneous.

00:30:40.311 --> 00:30:42.501
The convening of the causes and conditions

00:30:42.501 --> 00:30:46.901
of the opening of the cafe happen

00:30:46.901 --> 00:30:50.161
at the same time as the
opening of the cafe.

00:30:50.161 --> 00:30:52.138
Let's look at this puzzle.

00:30:52.138 --> 00:30:53.451
We just established, by the way,

00:30:53.451 --> 00:30:58.451
that they cannot come together
before the cafe opens.

00:30:58.538 --> 00:31:00.688
[instructor coughs]

00:31:00.688 --> 00:31:01.588
Now we look at,

00:31:01.588 --> 00:31:04.800
is it possible for them to
happen at the same time?

00:31:04.800 --> 00:31:06.810
Sorry. [Coughs] Sorry.

00:31:06.810 --> 00:31:10.477
,GAL TE TSOGS DANG LHAN CIG TU,

00:31:10.477 --> 00:31:12.224
,'BRAS BU YANG NI SKYE 'GYUR NA,.

00:31:12.224 --> 00:31:15.811
[Coughs] I'm sorry.

00:31:15.811 --> 00:31:19.761
If it were the case that the
result of the cafe opening

00:31:19.761 --> 00:31:21.100
popped up at the same time

00:31:21.100 --> 00:31:25.317
as the final payment came in for the loan,

00:31:26.937 --> 00:31:30.045
,SKYED PAR BYED DANG BSKYED BYA GANG,

00:31:30.045 --> 00:31:32.579
,DUS GCIG PAR NI THAL BAR 'GYUR,

00:31:32.579 --> 00:31:36.128
then the cause spitting out the result

00:31:36.128 --> 00:31:39.454
and the result spitted out by the cause

00:31:39.454 --> 00:31:42.091
should be simultaneous. Okay?

00:31:42.091 --> 00:31:45.128
If the convening of the
causes and conditions

00:31:45.128 --> 00:31:49.328
and the opening of the
cafe somehow overlapped,

00:31:49.328 --> 00:31:53.578
then you couldn't divide
the cause from the result.

00:31:54.654 --> 00:31:56.113
There would be no clear distinction

00:31:56.113 --> 00:31:58.464
between what was opening the cafe

00:31:58.464 --> 00:32:03.464
and the cafe being opened.

00:32:03.638 --> 00:32:05.180
GAL TE RGYU RKYEN GYI TSOGS PA NI 'BRAS BU

00:32:05.180 --> 00:32:07.029
DANG LHAN CIG SKYES PA NYID 'BRAS BU'I

00:32:07.029 --> 00:32:09.221
SKYED BYED DU 'GYUR RO ZHE NA,

00:32:09.221 --> 00:32:11.114
If it's the case that

00:32:13.738 --> 00:32:16.124
the convening of the causes
and conditions happens

00:32:16.124 --> 00:32:20.207
at the same time as the
coming out of the result.

00:32:22.324 --> 00:32:23.157
If you say that,

00:32:23.157 --> 00:32:24.557
GAL TE RGYU RKYEN GYI TSOGS PA DANG LHAN CIG TU

00:32:24.557 --> 00:32:26.123
'BRAS BU YANG NI SKYE BAR 'GYUR NA NI

00:32:26.123 --> 00:32:27.749
MI 'THAD DE

00:32:27.749 --> 00:32:31.661
It would be impossible,
it would be incorrect to say

00:32:31.661 --> 00:32:34.383
that the cafe opened at the same moment

00:32:34.383 --> 00:32:36.711
that everything you need
for the cafe to open

00:32:36.711 --> 00:32:38.560
finally came together.

00:32:38.560 --> 00:32:39.393
Why?

00:32:39.393 --> 00:32:41.426
SKYED PAR BYED PA RGYU DANG BSKYED PAR BYA BA

00:32:41.426 --> 00:32:43.059
'BRAS BU GANG YIN PA DE NI DUS GCIG TU

00:32:43.059 --> 00:32:45.402
YOD PAR NI THAL BAR 'GYUR BA'I PHYIR,

00:32:45.402 --> 00:32:47.911
In that case, they would
have to be simultaneous,

00:32:47.911 --> 00:32:51.711
the opening of the cafe
and the final moment

00:32:51.711 --> 00:32:55.101
of all the stuff needed
for the cafe to open,

00:32:55.101 --> 00:32:58.081
would be happening at the same time,

00:32:58.081 --> 00:33:01.236
probably the day before the cafe opened.

00:33:01.236 --> 00:33:02.236
Right, okay?

00:33:03.581 --> 00:33:05.631
DE LTAR MI RUNG STE, DUS MNYAM PA LA

00:33:05.631 --> 00:33:08.181
BSKYED BYA SKYED BYED MA
MTHONG BA'I PHYIR RO,,

00:33:08.181 --> 00:33:12.168
And that's incorrect
because we never see a case

00:33:12.168 --> 00:33:15.756
where the thing which produces an effect

00:33:15.756 --> 00:33:18.891
and the effect that is
produced by that thing

00:33:18.891 --> 00:33:20.737
are never simultaneous.

00:33:20.737 --> 00:33:23.767
There's always a time progression, right?

00:33:23.767 --> 00:33:26.991
First the cause happens
and then the result happens.

00:33:26.991 --> 00:33:29.493
It's not that they could be simultaneous.

00:33:29.493 --> 00:33:31.929
Okay.

00:33:31.929 --> 00:33:34.324
GSUM PA NI 
What's the third choice?

00:33:34.324 --> 00:33:37.159
This is the most interesting one to me.

00:33:37.159 --> 00:33:37.992
Yeah.

00:33:37.992 --> 00:33:40.289
The causes and conditions
for the cafe to open

00:33:40.289 --> 00:33:42.567
happen after the cafe opened.

00:33:42.567 --> 00:33:45.756
Which is what we were hoping.

00:33:45.756 --> 00:33:49.677
[instructor and students laugh]

00:33:49.677 --> 00:33:53.564
That's the one we've been
praying for, illogically.

00:33:53.564 --> 00:33:56.294
Okay, here we go.

00:33:56.294 --> 00:33:57.719
,GAL TE TSOGS PA'I SNGA ROL TU,

00:33:57.719 --> 00:33:59.485
,'BRAS BU SKYES PAR 'GYUR NA NI,

00:33:59.485 --> 00:34:00.326
,RGYU DANG RKYEN RNAMS MED PA NI,

00:34:00.326 --> 00:34:03.068
,'BRAS BU RGYU MED 'BYUNG BAR 'GYUR,

00:34:03.068 --> 00:34:07.746
,GAL TE TSOGS PA'I SNGA ROL TU,
If before the causes and conditions

00:34:07.746 --> 00:34:11.112
that finally came together

00:34:11.112 --> 00:34:12.620
,'BRAS BU SKYES PAR 'GYUR NA NI,

00:34:12.620 --> 00:34:14.113
If the cafe opened

00:34:16.364 --> 00:34:19.052
before the causes and
conditions were ready,

00:34:19.052 --> 00:34:22.269
,RGYU DANG RKYEN RNAMS MED PA NI,

00:34:22.269 --> 00:34:24.885
,'BRAS BU RGYU MED 'BYUNG BAR 'GYUR,

00:34:24.885 --> 00:34:26.696
then a result would have happened

00:34:26.696 --> 00:34:28.029
without a cause.

00:34:29.844 --> 00:34:34.473
If the cafe could open
before we got all the money,

00:34:34.473 --> 00:34:36.110
and the food, and all that,

00:34:36.110 --> 00:34:40.277
then you'd have a result
that didn't have a cause,

00:34:41.239 --> 00:34:42.898
which is what we are hoping for.

00:34:42.898 --> 00:34:43.731
Now,

00:34:45.325 --> 00:34:47.782
he goes to the Abhidharma school.

00:34:47.782 --> 00:34:49.313
And I thought it would be fun

00:34:49.313 --> 00:34:51.221
for you guys to go there.

00:34:51.221 --> 00:34:53.237
He goes to the Abhidharma school.

00:34:53.237 --> 00:34:55.445
I thought it would be
fun for us to go there.

00:34:55.445 --> 00:34:57.108
So, here we go.

00:34:57.108 --> 00:34:59.925
BYE BRAG SMRA BA NA RE,
'BRAS BU RNAMS RGYU RKYEN

00:34:59.925 --> 00:35:01.599
TSOGS PA'I SNGA
ROL GYI MA 'ONGS PA'I

00:35:01.599 --> 00:35:02.441
DUS SU GNAS PA YANG
YIN LA RGYU RKYEN TSOGS PAS NI

00:35:02.441 --> 00:35:03.274
DA LTA BA'I GNAS SKABS SKYED KYI,

00:35:03.274 --> 00:35:04.107
RDZAS NI SNGA PHYIR YANG GNAS SO ZHE NA,

00:35:11.840 --> 00:35:14.056
They have a special idea,

00:35:14.056 --> 00:35:15.770
and I believe is a reflection

00:35:15.770 --> 00:35:19.128
of the Sankya idea, okay?

00:35:19.128 --> 00:35:22.878
'BRAS BU RNAMS RGYU RKYEN
TSOGS PA'I SNGA ROL GYI

00:35:24.823 --> 00:35:29.073
The result of causes and
conditions coming together could...

00:35:34.732 --> 00:35:36.815
I got to think about this.

00:35:41.637 --> 00:35:44.033
Saying that the causes and conditions

00:35:44.033 --> 00:35:48.621
for the opening of the
cafe have come together

00:35:48.621 --> 00:35:51.871
is posited on the opening of the cafe.

00:35:55.033 --> 00:35:56.870
Therefore, the opening of the cafe

00:35:56.870 --> 00:35:59.017
did happen before the
causes and conditions

00:35:59.017 --> 00:36:02.701
of the opening of the cafe happened.

00:36:02.701 --> 00:36:07.368
It exists as a future certainty,
or something like that,

00:36:08.220 --> 00:36:11.387
which is a big discussion in Buddhism.

00:36:12.599 --> 00:36:15.687
If all the necessary causes
and conditions are present,

00:36:15.687 --> 00:36:19.514
could you even prevent
the opening of the cafe?

00:36:19.514 --> 00:36:22.872
Is it possible to prevent
the opening of the cafe?

00:36:22.872 --> 00:36:25.417
And we'd say "No." Okay?

00:36:25.417 --> 00:36:28.150
- Which causes and
conditions you're saying?

00:36:28.150 --> 00:36:31.461
- Oh, the causes and conditions
for the opening of the cafe.

00:36:31.461 --> 00:36:33.080
- Oh, are they causes and conditions

00:36:33.080 --> 00:36:34.805
of the opening of the cafe?

00:36:34.805 --> 00:36:35.638
- Yes.

00:36:35.638 --> 00:36:37.638
- So the cafe must be open

00:36:38.725 --> 00:36:40.320
while the causes and conditions are there,

00:36:40.320 --> 00:36:41.640
because they are causes and conditions

00:36:41.640 --> 00:36:43.512
for the opening of the cafe.

00:36:43.512 --> 00:36:48.512
The opening of the cafe owns
those causes and conditions.

00:36:48.723 --> 00:36:50.528
Therefore, the causes and conditions

00:36:50.528 --> 00:36:54.524
have to happen after
the opening of the cafe,

00:36:54.524 --> 00:36:56.260
because you can't call
them causes and conditions

00:36:56.260 --> 00:36:57.392
for the opening of the cafe,

00:36:57.392 --> 00:37:00.891
unless there is an opening of the cafe.

00:37:00.891 --> 00:37:04.659
And this is true. And this
goes back to an ancient point

00:37:04.659 --> 00:37:08.909
made in the first ACI course,
with the spear analogy.

00:37:10.907 --> 00:37:11.990
When soldiers

00:37:14.867 --> 00:37:17.669
get home from fighting all day in battle,

00:37:17.669 --> 00:37:19.247
they would sit down for their meal

00:37:19.247 --> 00:37:23.497
after they put their spears,
stack them together

00:37:25.045 --> 00:37:29.391
in a tripod. This is
the ancient example.

00:37:29.391 --> 00:37:31.339
They come home from a
hard day of fighting,

00:37:31.339 --> 00:37:33.979
they're going to sit
down and have some pizza,

00:37:33.979 --> 00:37:36.364
and they stack their spears.

00:37:36.364 --> 00:37:38.807
They have their spears point up,

00:37:38.807 --> 00:37:41.996
resting on each other
like a tripod, and that's

00:37:41.996 --> 00:37:44.569
because if the enemy
suddenly shows up for pizza,

00:37:44.569 --> 00:37:47.443
they can grab their spear quickly

00:37:47.443 --> 00:37:49.620
and start poking people.

00:37:49.620 --> 00:37:54.620
And the analogy in Pabongka
Rinpoche's commentary

00:37:54.745 --> 00:37:58.540
to "The Three Principal Paths",
which I'm sure you remember

00:37:58.540 --> 00:38:02.790
from ACI Course One, is that

00:38:05.288 --> 00:38:08.511
it is true that results depend on causes

00:38:08.511 --> 00:38:11.594
but causes equally depend on results,

00:38:12.702 --> 00:38:14.428
because they cannot be called causes

00:38:14.428 --> 00:38:18.124
until the result has come out.

00:38:18.124 --> 00:38:21.160
You can't call the investment money

00:38:21.160 --> 00:38:23.689
of the opening the cafe

00:38:23.689 --> 00:38:27.420
the investment money for
the opening of the cafe,

00:38:27.420 --> 00:38:30.720
it cannot be called the cause
for the opening of the cafe

00:38:30.720 --> 00:38:33.096
until the cafe opens.

00:38:33.096 --> 00:38:35.150
Then you can say it's a cause

00:38:35.150 --> 00:38:37.815
because otherwise there's
no opening of the cafe

00:38:37.815 --> 00:38:39.432
that had the cause.

00:38:39.432 --> 00:38:40.423
Got it?

00:38:40.423 --> 00:38:42.291
It can't be a cause for
the opening of the cafe

00:38:42.291 --> 00:38:44.163
until there is an opening of the cafe.

00:38:44.163 --> 00:38:47.199
Only when the cafe opens
and there's a result

00:38:47.199 --> 00:38:48.959
can you say it had a cause.

00:38:48.959 --> 00:38:52.400
Before the cafe opens, it's just a thing

00:38:52.400 --> 00:38:53.919
that's going on.

00:38:53.919 --> 00:38:56.502
It doesn't have a second half.

00:38:56.502 --> 00:38:59.319
Once the second half is
complete, the result,

00:38:59.319 --> 00:39:03.444
then the money, the
food, Rosa's effort, they

00:39:03.444 --> 00:39:05.292
can be called causes,

00:39:05.292 --> 00:39:09.535
but only after the result comes out.

00:39:09.535 --> 00:39:11.443
So they're kind of going there. Who?

00:39:11.443 --> 00:39:13.282
The Abhidharmists.

00:39:13.282 --> 00:39:14.115
RGYU RKYEN TSOGS PAS NI

00:39:14.115 --> 00:39:17.948
DA LTA BA'I GNAS SKABS SKYED KYI,

00:39:17.948 --> 00:39:18.781
RDZAS NI

00:39:18.781 --> 00:39:20.444
SNGA PHYIR YANG GNAS SO

00:39:20.444 --> 00:39:23.060
So in that sense, the opening of the cafe

00:39:23.060 --> 00:39:26.171
did exist during the convening

00:39:26.171 --> 00:39:27.847
of its causes and conditions.

00:39:27.847 --> 00:39:29.695
Otherwise you couldn't have called them

00:39:29.695 --> 00:39:31.844
conditions for the opening.

00:39:31.844 --> 00:39:35.230
There must have been some kind
of opening of cafe around

00:39:35.230 --> 00:39:37.914
for these things to be called
the causes and conditions

00:39:37.914 --> 00:39:40.247
for the opening of the cafe.

00:39:42.857 --> 00:39:46.439
Then we say 
DE NI MI RIGS TE

00:39:46.439 --> 00:39:48.223
"Hey, that's dumb."

00:39:48.223 --> 00:39:51.213
John Brady is the only
one who was doubting it.

00:39:51.213 --> 00:39:54.656
Now, you're correct.

00:39:54.656 --> 00:39:55.923
That's not right.

00:39:55.923 --> 00:39:57.756
GAL TE RGYU RKYEN GYI TSOGS PA'I 
SNGA ROL DU
792
00:39:57,756 --&gt; 00:39:57,589
'BRAS BU SKYES PA
STE GRUB PAR GYUR NA NI,

00:40:00.091 --> 00:40:02.377
If the result of the cafe opening

00:40:02.377 --> 00:40:05.744
were somehow to be present
before the causes and conditions

00:40:05.744 --> 00:40:06.577
were finally brought together,

00:40:06.577 --> 00:40:07.410
'BRAS BU DE RGYU DANG RKYEN RNAMS LA

00:40:07.410 --> 00:40:08.243
BLTOS PA MED PAR 'GYUR

00:40:11.520 --> 00:40:13.435
That result would no longer rely

00:40:13.435 --> 00:40:17.685
upon those causes and
conditions for its existence.

00:40:19.551 --> 00:40:22.234
If the cafe opening existed

00:40:22.234 --> 00:40:24.819
during the time of the
causes and conditions,

00:40:24.819 --> 00:40:27.932
then we would have to say,
that the opening of the cafe

00:40:27.932 --> 00:40:31.067
was not contingent upon
those causes and conditions

00:40:31.067 --> 00:40:35.234
because it was even there
before they could begin.

00:40:36.424 --> 00:40:41.424
If they are simultaneous,
there's no dependence.

00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:42.393
Okay?

00:40:49.468 --> 00:40:50.301
DE LTA NA DE YI 'BRAS BU
RGYU MED PAR 'BYUNG BA

00:40:50.301 --> 00:40:51.134
CAN DU 'GYUR BA'I SKYON YOD PA'I PHYIR

00:40:52.580 --> 00:40:56.578
And in that case, you could
have an opening of the cafe

00:40:56.578 --> 00:40:59.048
before you had the causes and conditions.

00:40:59.048 --> 00:41:02.131
And then where's the causation there?

00:41:07.388 --> 00:41:08.661
Hang in there. Okay?

00:41:08.661 --> 00:41:10.984
Don't you say, "Oh,
this is stupid, I'll go

00:41:10.984 --> 00:41:13.208
on to Lam Rim or something."

00:41:13.208 --> 00:41:15.540
Don't think like that.

00:41:15.540 --> 00:41:18.048
Struggle with it. What's
the worst that can happen?

00:41:18.048 --> 00:41:19.631
We covered it today.

00:41:21.884 --> 00:41:24.360
You get born into a world
were there's no Buddhism

00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:28.978
but you're the only one
who figures everything out.

00:41:28.978 --> 00:41:30.740
That's the worst that can happen.

00:41:30.740 --> 00:41:31.905
All right.

00:41:31.905 --> 00:41:32.738
GNYIS PA LA GNYIS, RGYU
'BRAS NGO BO GCIG PA'I

00:41:32.738 --> 00:41:33.571
PHYOGS DGAG PA DANG, NGO BO
THA DAD PA'I PHYOGS DGAG PA

00:41:43.008 --> 00:41:46.087
Is a cause and its result one thing?

00:41:46.087 --> 00:41:49.587
Or is a cause and its
result separate things?

00:41:50.652 --> 00:41:52.224
This is an old...

00:41:52.224 --> 00:41:55.476
You're all like 
"Oh, that's Utpala's book."

00:41:55.476 --> 00:41:56.988
We already know the answer to that

00:41:56.988 --> 00:41:59.148
but I don't remember."
[students laugh]

00:41:59.148 --> 00:42:01.731
Okay.

00:42:03.128 --> 00:42:06.440
Is it true that to be the
cause is to be the result?

00:42:06.440 --> 00:42:08.273
Or is it the case that

00:42:09.561 --> 00:42:12.711
to be the cause is to be
different from the result?

00:42:12.711 --> 00:42:14.471
That's the question.

00:42:14.471 --> 00:42:16.909
And we're going to cover
the first possibility.

00:42:16.909 --> 00:42:20.316
Is it true that to be the
cause is to be the result?

00:42:20.316 --> 00:42:21.596
Here's the verse.

00:42:21.596 --> 00:42:23.429
,GAL TE RGYU 'GAGS 'BRAS BU NA,

00:42:23.429 --> 00:42:25.262
,RGYU NI KUN DU 'PHO BAR 'GYUR,

00:42:25.262 --> 00:42:27.095
,SNGON SKYES PA YI RGYU YANG NI,

00:42:27.095 --> 00:42:29.928
,YANG SKYE BAR NI THAL BAR 'GYUR,

00:42:29.928 --> 00:42:31.761
GAL TE RGYU ‘GAGS NAS

00:42:31.761 --> 00:42:33.594
‘BRAS BU’I BDAG NYID DU 

00:42:33.594 --> 00:42:34.827
GNAS PA YIN NO

00:42:34.827 --> 00:42:37.410
This is an interesting concept.

00:42:39.300 --> 00:42:41.133
And it's called 'PHO BA.

00:42:42.072 --> 00:42:44.372
And here's another meaning
of the word 'PHO BA,

00:42:44.372 --> 00:42:46.979
but it's similar. You can tell.

00:42:46.979 --> 00:42:49.146
Someone comes up and says,

00:42:50.728 --> 00:42:52.576
how do you say it?

00:42:52.576 --> 00:42:55.826
"The cause transforms into the result."

00:42:57.583 --> 00:42:59.783
Okay, you don't have
to talk about the cause

00:42:59.783 --> 00:43:01.708
starting, stopping and then the result

00:43:01.708 --> 00:43:04.433
either starting, or stopping,
or somehow they overlap.

00:43:04.433 --> 00:43:06.216
You don't have to talk like that.

00:43:06.216 --> 00:43:09.331
The cause transforms into the result.

00:43:09.331 --> 00:43:12.243
Which is a reasonable
way to say it. Right?

00:43:12.243 --> 00:43:15.910
So in Nagarjuna's literature,
it is called 'PHO BA.

00:43:16.895 --> 00:43:19.978
'PHO BA usually refers to what? For us.

00:43:21.079 --> 00:43:21.912
- [Student 1] Change of life?

00:43:21.912 --> 00:43:23.618
- Yeah, you change lifetimes.

00:43:23.618 --> 00:43:25.083
You change rebirth. Right?

00:43:25.083 --> 00:43:28.183
You move from one
rebirth to another.

00:43:28.183 --> 00:43:33.183
And here he's talking about
the identity of the cause

00:43:33.287 --> 00:43:36.127
shifting into an identity as a result,

00:43:36.127 --> 00:43:39.119
but it's the same thing.

00:43:39.119 --> 00:43:43.831
It's one person who used to
be Bob and changed to John.

00:43:43.831 --> 00:43:45.811
But it's the same person.

00:43:45.811 --> 00:43:50.811
The result is the cause in
different clothes. [giggles]

00:43:54.110 --> 00:43:58.610
The cause changed its pants
and that's called result.

00:43:59.611 --> 00:44:01.526
But it's still the cause.

00:44:01.526 --> 00:44:03.826
He just changed his pants.

00:44:03.826 --> 00:44:05.597
[laughs] Okay, all right.

00:44:05.597 --> 00:44:07.454
That's an interesting idea.

00:44:07.454 --> 00:44:09.909
Let's see what Nagarjuna says.

00:44:09.909 --> 00:44:11.041
Are we okay on time?

00:44:11.041 --> 00:44:13.580
Time, Tim? Time, Tim, Tim, time?

00:44:13.580 --> 00:44:15.726
Five more minutes. Let's
see how much we can do.

00:44:15.726 --> 00:44:18.202
DE NI MI 'THAD DE
I don't like that.

00:44:18.202 --> 00:44:22.593
GAL TE RGYU 'GAGS NAS 'BRAS
BU'I BDAG NYID DU 'PHO NA

00:44:22.593 --> 00:44:25.760
So are you saying that the cause stops

00:44:29.429 --> 00:44:31.814
and then transforms into the result?

00:44:31.814 --> 00:44:33.278
Is that what you're saying?

00:44:33.278 --> 00:44:35.346
The cause comes to an end

00:44:35.346 --> 00:44:39.086
and then it slips into
result and kind of changes?

00:44:39.086 --> 00:44:42.287
Is that what you're saying
when you say 'PHO BA?

00:44:42.287 --> 00:44:45.311
Is that what you mean when
you say "moves"? Okay?

00:44:45.311 --> 00:44:46.784
Transfers?

00:44:46.784 --> 00:44:50.658
Transitions into result?
Is that what you're saying?

00:44:50.658 --> 00:44:51.866
And the guy says, "Yeah."

00:44:51.866 --> 00:44:52.699
And then he says, "Well it sounds...

00:44:52.699 --> 00:44:53.532
ZLOS GAR MKHAN CHA LUGS GZHAN

00:44:53.532 --> 00:44:54.365
DANG GZHAN DU BSGYUR

00:44:57.142 --> 00:44:58.913
Can you put that up on the screen?

00:44:58.913 --> 00:45:00.246
It's kind of cute.

00:45:02.577 --> 00:45:03.656
Second, yeah.

00:45:03.656 --> 00:45:07.053
ZLOS GAR MKHAN CHA LUGS
GZHAN DANG GZHAN DU BSGYUR

00:45:07.053 --> 00:45:08.970
Is a beautiful example.

00:45:10.325 --> 00:45:14.742
ZLOS GAR means the ancient
Sanskrit and Tibet dramas

00:45:16.793 --> 00:45:19.025
which were acted out on a small stage,

00:45:19.025 --> 00:45:22.821
like the Greek comedies,
and the Greek dramas.

00:45:22.821 --> 00:45:23.988
ZLOS GAR means

00:45:28.472 --> 00:45:29.555
a stage play,

00:45:30.525 --> 00:45:33.993
like the classical Greek
tragedies and things like that.

00:45:33.993 --> 00:45:37.048
It's called ZLOS GAR.

00:45:37.048 --> 00:45:41.683
ZLOS GAR MKHAN means an actor
in one of those plays.

00:45:41.683 --> 00:45:44.156
So let's take an actor
in one of those plays.

00:45:44.156 --> 00:45:46.679
CHA LUGS GZHAN DANG GZHAN DU BSGYUR

00:45:46.679 --> 00:45:51.363
So you're saying when a
cause produces a result

00:45:51.363 --> 00:45:56.363
it's like the actor was playing
one character in the first act

00:45:58.975 --> 00:46:01.210
and then he ran backstage
and changed clothes

00:46:01.210 --> 00:46:03.158
and came out in the second act,

00:46:03.158 --> 00:46:05.489
and played a different character.

00:46:05.489 --> 00:46:09.117
Is a beautiful example,
because it kind of is the...

00:46:09.117 --> 00:46:12.366
That's the picture we have when
he described 'PHO BA, right?

00:46:12.366 --> 00:46:16.522
The cause put on different
pants and became the result.

00:46:16.522 --> 00:46:18.174
It's the same idea.

00:46:18.174 --> 00:46:23.174
The same thing, essentially,
put on a different outfit

00:46:23.278 --> 00:46:26.025
and came out as a different actor,

00:46:26.025 --> 00:46:28.963
but it's the same guy.

00:46:28.963 --> 00:46:31.471
The cause and the result are the same guy

00:46:31.471 --> 00:46:36.138
in different costumes during
different acts of the play.

00:46:39.177 --> 00:46:40.072
Is that what you're saying?

00:46:40.072 --> 00:46:43.857
RGYU NI DUS KUN DU 'PHO
BA TZAM DU 'GYUR GYI,

00:46:43.857 --> 00:46:47.862
So you're saying causes
just kind of change

00:46:47.862 --> 00:46:52.051
their outer appearance
and become results, right?

00:46:52.051 --> 00:46:52.884
'BRAS BU SNGAR MED GSAR DU

00:46:52.884 --> 00:46:53.717
MI SKYE BAR 'GYUR BA'I PHYIR TE,

00:46:56.155 --> 00:47:00.488
So are you saying a new
result has come out or not?

00:47:01.784 --> 00:47:05.163
DE LTA NA RGYU DE RTAG PAR 'GYUR BAS

00:47:05.163 --> 00:47:09.410
That's an interesting idea. If the result

00:47:09.410 --> 00:47:13.523
is the power of the cause
dressed up in different clothes,

00:47:13.523 --> 00:47:17.747
then the cause hasn't really
changed in its essence.

00:47:17.747 --> 00:47:20.498
It's just put on new clothes.

00:47:20.498 --> 00:47:24.018
And in that case, what was
there at 3:00

00:47:24.018 --> 00:47:26.186
is still there at 3:01.

00:47:26.186 --> 00:47:28.847
And in that case, it's 
RTAG PA

00:47:28.847 --> 00:47:31.686
What does that mean? It's unchanging.

00:47:31.686 --> 00:47:34.759
It's an unchanging functioning thing,

00:47:34.759 --> 00:47:37.603
which is a four letter word.

00:47:37.603 --> 00:47:39.790
- [Student 2] I though of the word fixed.

00:47:39.790 --> 00:47:41.243
- Fixed?
- [Student 2] It's fixed.

00:47:41.243 --> 00:47:43.355
- Yeah, you can say fixed.

00:47:43.355 --> 00:47:46.655
But you know, in classical Buddhism,

00:47:46.655 --> 00:47:49.735
it's almost like saying a dirty word.

00:47:49.735 --> 00:47:53.487
When you say "This thing does something,

00:47:53.487 --> 00:47:56.875
but by doing something
it doesn't change."

00:47:56.875 --> 00:48:00.068
That's totally illegal
in all of Buddhism.

00:48:00.068 --> 00:48:02.389
So if you're going to say,
"The cause is the result

00:48:02.389 --> 00:48:04.338
in different clothes,"

00:48:04.338 --> 00:48:07.682
then what you're talking
about is cause and effect

00:48:07.682 --> 00:48:11.691
where nothing changes.
It's just impossible.

00:48:11.691 --> 00:48:14.524
It's totally against all Buddhism.

00:48:15.654 --> 00:48:18.516
We're going to stop there

00:48:18.516 --> 00:48:21.253
because everyone has a headache.

00:48:21.253 --> 00:48:23.336
[students laugh]

00:48:23.336 --> 00:48:24.836
Oh, one more line.

00:48:29.122 --> 00:48:32.672
The other option is that the
cause that changes its clothes

00:48:32.672 --> 00:48:37.672
and becomes the result, would
just keep changing its clothes,

00:48:40.824 --> 00:48:44.948
and then it would be an
infinite regression.

00:48:44.948 --> 00:48:46.656
So that's called 
THUG MED

00:48:46.656 --> 00:48:49.087
THUG MED PA is an idea in Buddhism

00:48:49.087 --> 00:48:49.920
that the same thing would just...

00:48:49.920 --> 00:48:50.753
there's no reason why it
shouldn't just keep happening

00:48:52.946 --> 00:48:56.280
over and over again, endlessly.

00:48:56.280 --> 00:48:59.668
So I don't know, a peach tree
seed creates a peach tree,

00:48:59.668 --> 00:49:01.340
and then it creates another peach tree,

00:49:01.340 --> 00:49:03.162
and it creates another
peach tree, and so on.

00:49:03.162 --> 00:49:04.880
Because it's all the same seed

00:49:04.880 --> 00:49:06.770
in different clothing.

00:49:06.770 --> 00:49:08.687
Okay. Where are we now?

00:49:13.810 --> 00:49:16.476
Next up, in the next class,

00:49:16.476 --> 00:49:20.143
it's a very interesting
extended discussion

00:49:21.416 --> 00:49:24.083
of seven different possibilities

00:49:25.650 --> 00:49:29.650
of how a cause gets ready
to trigger a result.

00:49:31.076 --> 00:49:34.496
So we're going to get
seven different ideas

00:49:34.496 --> 00:49:38.413
about how a cause warms
up to produce a result.

00:49:40.225 --> 00:49:43.715
And there's a very interesting discussion

00:49:43.715 --> 00:49:46.298
of all the possible variations

00:49:47.730 --> 00:49:51.730
on how does a cause warm
up to produce a result.

00:49:54.911 --> 00:49:57.454
And what does that look like?

00:49:57.454 --> 00:50:00.193
We're going to discuss seven
different possibilities.

00:50:00.193 --> 00:50:02.451
They're all impossible.

00:50:02.451 --> 00:50:04.847
All seven possibilities are impossible.

00:50:04.847 --> 00:50:06.444
And we'll go to that next.

00:50:06.444 --> 00:50:10.111
Just to set you up, let
me make a mark here.

00:50:13.484 --> 00:50:18.484
I want to give you some hope.

00:50:21.776 --> 00:50:25.169
That's going to lead us
on to chapter 21.

00:50:25.169 --> 00:50:29.085
So we'll be running to discuss
another topic after that.

00:50:29.085 --> 00:50:30.549
So hang in there.

00:50:30.549 --> 00:50:33.749
We'll talk about seven different ways

00:50:33.749 --> 00:50:37.601
in which a cause warms
up to produce a result.

00:50:37.601 --> 00:50:40.161
And then we'll get free from this chapter

00:50:40.161 --> 00:50:43.239
and we'll go to another
chapter very quickly.

00:50:43.239 --> 00:50:44.705
[student laughs]

00:50:44.705 --> 00:50:45.916
All right? Okay.

